2|0@asoiaf^1440882473#cuk2qn6:NematodeArthritis$:It's likely that Damascus steel was GRRM's major inspiration for Valyrian steel. Though the original formula/technique for crafting Damascus steel has been lost to the ages, the modern technique of pattern-welding steel replicates the original look very closely, and can be [really beautiful](http://imgur.com/0Qv9zRR). I've got a few pattern-welded knives myself. Bought them because they're beautiful, but also because I really wanted something I could say inspired Valyrian steel.
3|0@asoiaf^1440882688#cuk2usf:fixius60$:It's easily made today. It isn't a secret. The only confusion stems from people who believe the exaggerated claims about how the 'ancients' could make Damascus steel that was soooo sharps that it cut through mega ninja TRex bones. So yeah we lost the recipe for the magic katana Damascus. In reality it was a labor intensive steel that was amazing for the time. But modern day steels are far superior in every way. If you search around you can find all kinds of videos about how it's made. 
